  "body": "Addendum to my hand-off memo filed 2026-05-23-0900. PO surfaced a sharpening 2026-05-23 ~10:30 EDT that re-categorizes most of what I handed off. The sharpening: the -defs (catdef, roledef, orgdef, memodef, transcriptdef) are about DATA FORMATS — substrate-shaped specs for how organizational state is encoded as data. OAGP is an ORGANIZATIONAL PATTERN — the shape of an org that uses AI peers as first-class participants with bounded authority, ratification cycles, role-binding, audit trails, async/scheduled operation, adoption-cycle primitives. The pattern requires SOME data substrate but isn't specifically the -def stack; you could imagine OAGP-on-protobuf or OAGP-on-XML. catdef family is the recommended canonical substrate because it's also AI-peer-aware (schema-as-data); the recommendation is for substrate-AI-peer-alignment, not because OAGP requires catdef. Implications: (a) oagp-org needs to exist as its own home — PO is scaffolding it now while I file this; (b) most of what I handed off is OAGP-pattern-shape work, properly belonging to oagp-strategist (when staffed) rather than orgdef-strategist; (c) you retain anything actually orgdef-format-shape (orgdef schema changes, positions/relationships structure changes); (d) the bootstrap+onboard skills + agent-runner + plugin + canonical hosting all migrate to oagp-org and become oagp-strategist work. Re-categorization table in §3 of body. Recommendation: hold the OAGP-pattern items I handed off; re-route to oagp-strategist (or to PO as oagp-director until staffed) once oagp-org exists. Apologies for the mid-stream re-routing; the data-vs-pattern distinction wasn't legible to me yesterday but is now.",
